From 03a6252f3eb1df9470b761dc5148a1b16452e6b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:44:58 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Link through libtool with $(LTLIBINTL), not $(LIBINTL)

configure.ac put $LIBINTL in the global LIBS, but every target is linked
through libtool. When gettext's lib-link macros find libintl outside the
default prefix (as in an aarch64-pc-cygwin cross build, where the
libintl prefix is the sysroot), LIBINTL is the absolute path
.../libintl.dll.a. libtool --mode=link for a shared library treats an
absolute *.a argument as a static archive and only keeps it when
deplibs_check_method is pass_all or match_pattern; Cygwin's file_magic
method drops it with "Trying to link with static lib archive", and
libblkid.la then fails to link with undefined libintl_gettext.

LTLIBINTL is the form gettext provides for libtool (-L<dir> -lintl), and
it is what Makefile.am already uses for LDADD. Natively it is -lintl or
empty, so native builds are unchanged. The generated configure gets the
same one-line change.

Signed-off-by: aswin-mcw <aswin.kalies@multicorewareinc.com>
---
 configure    | 2 +-
 configure.ac | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 3ceee78..e9784c5 100644
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -45278,7 +45278,7 @@ printf "%s\n" "$as_me: setting link_all_deplibs=unknown for libtool" >&6;}
 fi
 
 
-LIBS="$LIBINTL"
+LIBS="$LTLIBINTL"
 
 
 ac_config_headers="$ac_config_headers config.h"
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index 6e2b593..1fd7804 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -2943,7 +2943,7 @@ if test "x${build_alias}" != "x${host_alias}"; then
 fi
 
 
-LIBS="$LIBINTL"
+LIBS="$LTLIBINTL"
 
 
 AC_CONFIG_HEADERS([config.h])
